{"data": [{"author_id": "1454021186061410309", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:02:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117724037606519240"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 215, "start": 204, "tag": "OpenSource"}, {"end": 219, "start": 216, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 236, "start": 220, "tag": "MachineLearning"}]}, "id": "2117724037606519240", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Frontier AI on your gaming PC: Berkeley engineers released FreeToken, an engine running 290B MoE models on consumer rigs. Devs can now run frontier reasoning locally without renting expensive cloud GPUs. #OpenSource #AI #MachineLearning", "url": "https://x.com/FlashAllTech/status/2117724037606519240"}, {"author_id": "167432266", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:41:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117733855020917142"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 225, "start": 216, "tag": "AIPolicy"}, {"end": 249, "start": 226, "tag": "ArtificialIntelligence"}]}, "id": "2117733855020917142", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Anthropic has quietly pitched its own AI safety bill to U.S. lawmakers, targeting only the most advanced frontier AI models that could pose serious risks. This could be a pivotal moment for AI regulation in America. #AIPolicy #ArtificialIntelligence", "url": "https://x.com/NewsRamp_Alerts/status/2117733855020917142"}, {"author_id": "1041829807011627009", "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:59:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117723429793411374"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 258, "start": 249, "tag": "AISafety"}, {"end": 262, "start": 259, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"description": "Beth Barnes, Founder and CEO at METR: sourced bio, career timeline. Fields: Evaluation and benchmarks, Safety and alignment.", "display_url": "aipeoplewiki.com/people/beth-ba…", "end": 247, "expanded_url": "https://aipeoplewiki.com/people/beth-barnes/?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=spotlight", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117723432679026688/e21n3Pl-?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117723432679026688/e21n3Pl-?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 224, "status": 200, "title": "Beth Barnes Wiki: Founder and CEO at METR | AI People Wiki", "unwound_url": "https://aipeoplewiki.com/people/beth-barnes/?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=spotlight", "url": "https://t.co/EcUVK867t0"}]}, "id": "2117723429793411374", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Spotlight on Beth Barnes, founder and CEO of METR, the research nonprofit that evaluates what frontier AI models can do on their own. Co-author of RE-Bench and METR's study on AI completing long software tasks. Great work!\n\nhttps://t.co/EcUVK867t0\n\n#AISafety #AI", "url": "https://x.com/Shadowfetch/status/2117723429793411374"}, {"author_id": "1914378015733374977", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:01:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117723882576822591"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/qb6tvRuaUJ", "end": 282, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Aligned_SI/status/2117723882576822591/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117723823231602688", "start": 259, "url": "https://t.co/qb6tvRuaUJ"}]}, "id": "2117723882576822591", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Congress is weighing new safeguards for frontier AI, but the bigger question is whether we can keep pace with its growing capabilities. \n\nWe need both effective oversight and technical solutions that keep SuperIntelligence safe and aligned with human values. https://t.co/qb6tvRuaUJ", "url": "https://x.com/Aligned_SI/status/2117723882576822591"}, {"author_id": "781585690618388482", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:32:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117731763275313538"], "id": "2117731763275313538", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "OpenAI and Anthropic just triggered an all-out price war, cutting new model API costs by up to 50%.\n\n​The era of charging whatever you want for raw model benchmarks is officially over.\n\n​When every top lab can deliver near-frontier reasoning, the winning moat isn't just", "url": "https://x.com/VujuOnX/status/2117731763275313538"}, {"author_id": "2091978331126116352", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:33:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117732031736217982"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 25, "start": 20, "tag": "PLTR"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/9S184AxvBl", "end": 214, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/KilianCuxus/status/2117732031736217982/video/1", "media_key": "13_2117731959895957504", "start": 191, "url": "https://t.co/9S184AxvBl"}]}, "id": "2117732031736217982", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "What does Palantir ($PLTR) actually sell?\nThe Ontology: a digital twin of an organization that lets people, and now AI, act on real data within rules and permissions.\nExplained in 5 minutes. https://t.co/9S184AxvBl", "url": "https://x.com/KilianCuxus/status/2117732031736217982"}, {"author_id": "2089726691652341760", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:51:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117736325155831811"], "id": "2117736325155831811", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "EU AI Act compliance shouldn't require a €100k consultancy—or guesswork. I built Proofbough to help European SMBs inventory AI, assess risk, create practical documentation, train staff, and stay audit-ready. Practical AI governance without the enterprise price tag.", "url": "https://x.com/newonpolsia/status/2117736325155831811"}, {"author_id": "2089726691652341760", "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:54:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117722201059373460"], "id": "2117722201059373460", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Most SMBs use AI without a clear record of where, which vendors, or what risks are involved. Built Meldmark to fix that: inventory AI use, document risks and policies, and track requirements like the EU AI Act and Canadian proposals. Live soon.", "url": "https://x.com/newonpolsia/status/2117722201059373460"}, {"author_id": "2115594718293671936", "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:56:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117722565150167130"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "White Hat Labs maps the 63 MITRE ATLAS agent runtime techniques to EU AI Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689), with the detection patterns and measurements behind them.", "display_url": "whitehatlabs.ai/research/atlas…", "end": 255, "expanded_url": "https://whitehatlabs.ai/research/atlas-eu-ai-act", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117722571785523200/pClleaBm?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117722571785523200/pClleaBm?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 232, "status": 200, "title": "MITRE ATLAS to EU AI Act", "unwound_url": "https://whitehatlabs.ai/research/atlas-eu-ai-act", "url": "https://t.co/bvUZkY0ScF"}]}, "id": "2117722565150167130", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "EU AI Act Art. 15: high-risk AI must resist third parties altering its use, outputs or performance. For agents, that is prompt injection.\n\nArt. 12 adds automatic event logs. We mapped 56 of 63 MITRE ATLAS agent attacks to Art. 15.\n\nhttps://t.co/bvUZkY0ScF", "url": "https://x.com/WhiteHatLabsAI/status/2117722565150167130"}, {"author_id": "2234985075", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:09:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117725982228357559"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/TQvow8ZrJt", "end": 306, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/VukRosic99/status/2117725982228357559/video/1", "media_key": "13_2117722660784246784", "start": 283, "url": "https://t.co/TQvow8ZrJt"}]}, "id": "2117725982228357559", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 147, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "How to use AI for papers\n\nDesign environments and benchmarks and baselines first, then let it auto-research.\n\n&gt; build the environment and evals first, have AI act as the ICML reviewer until no issues are left, test with 5 second runs, then let it design and test new modules. The https://t.co/TQvow8ZrJt", "url": "https://x.com/VukRosic99/status/2117725982228357559"}, {"author_id": "1983916015877812224", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:07:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117725257029365955"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 4, "start": 0, "tag": "SPY"}, {"end": 166, "start": 161, "tag": "NVDA"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/4VZHGl7Qlf", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MilkRoadAI/status/2117725257029365955/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117725254659588096", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/4VZHGl7Qlf"}, {"display_url": "x.com/20676401281058…", "end": 324, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/2067640128105824256/status/2116285655814897681", "start": 301, "url": "https://t.co/JN8ydL3Trw"}]}, "id": "2117725257029365955", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1261, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "211628